---
source: tests/cli_golden.rs
expression: help
---
Disable a plugin in `AURA_HOME/config.toml` (`enabled = false`)

Usage: aura plugins disable [OPTIONS] <ID>

Arguments:
  <ID>
          Plugin id (matches the manifest `id` field)

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          Session mode for the interactive terminal. Overrides the daemon default (`AURA_DEFAULT_MODE`); the kernel denies any tool call the mode does not allow

          Possible values:
          - agent: Full unrestricted operation subject to user permissions
          - plan:  Read + markdown writes + read-only subprocesses
          - ask:   Read-only
          - debug: Read + sandboxed probes only

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
